cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis code or the derived data tables, please cite the archived release and the associated article."
type: software
title: "What transfers and what does not: cross-platform evaluation of a fixed immune–metabolic transcriptional score for breast cancer overall survival"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a fixed 14-gene immune-metabolic
  transcriptional score evaluated across breast cancer cohorts. The score was
  derived in GSE42568 and evaluated supportively in GSE20685; the model-lock and
  initial GSE20685 analysis share a commit, so their order is unresolved.
  Subsequent commits document application of fixed parameters without refitting
  to SCAN-B GSE96058 (RNA-seq) and METABRIC (Illumina HT-12). Positive
  cohort-level average per-SD associations were observed, but METABRIC showed a
  late directional reversal; the absolute cutoff did not transport. PAM50 heterogeneity in SCAN-B was
  exploratory and post hoc and was not reproduced in the broader METABRIC
  CLAUDIN_SUBTYPE analysis.
